    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-2-sec-4-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (2) does not:  (a) have the effect that, merely because such evidence to the contrary is adduced, the person who made the representation is taken to have had reasonable grounds for making the representation; or  (b) have the effect of placing on any person an onus of proving that the person who made the representation had reasonable grounds for making the representation.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits an action.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) To avoid doubt, subsection (2) does not:  (a) have the effect that, merely because such evidence to the contrary is adduced, the person who made the representation is taken to have had reasonable grounds for making the representation; or  (b) have the effect of placing on any person an onus of proving that the person who made the representation had reasonable grounds for making the representation."
    },
